<%--
Rsx_Error_Dialog

The framework's own error dialog: what an Ajax failure nobody caught shows when the
application registered no error dialog of its own (Rsx.set_ajax_error_handler()). It is in
every bundle - SPA, Blade, the /_sys panel - so no page fails silently, and it depends on
no theme: core has no palette, so its look is self-contained (Rsx_Error_Dialog.scss) and
sits in the framework's reserved z-index range for uncaught-error displays.

    await Rsx_Error_Dialog.show_error(error);   // an Ajax Error, as the transport shows it
    await Rsx_Error_Dialog.show({title, message, detail});

$title    the heading
$message  the sentence to show (line breaks kept)
$detail   optional preformatted developer detail (file, line, trace) - present only when the
          server admitted the caller as a developer
$on_close called once when the dialog is closed (Close, Escape)
--%>
<Define:Rsx_Error_Dialog tag="div">
    <div class="Rsx_Error_Dialog__box">
        <div class="Rsx_Error_Dialog__title" $sid="title"><%= this.args.title %></div>
        <div class="Rsx_Error_Dialog__message"><%br= this.args.message %></div>
        <% if (this.args.detail) { %>
            <pre class="Rsx_Error_Dialog__detail"><%= this.args.detail %></pre>
        <% } %>
        <div class="Rsx_Error_Dialog__actions">
            <button type="button" class="Rsx_Error_Dialog__close" $sid="close">Close</button>
        </div>
    </div>
</Define:Rsx_Error_Dialog>
